e these letters  are a bright yellow so they get your  attention  and it's a good letter it's a well  written letter i said about 20 i agree  with that and i would say  half of those are just politely telling  you  right yeah 20 of people will respond to  you and some of them will just respond  and say  hey thanks for your message but right  now we're not interested in selling it's  like 10 isn't it  one ten one in ten ten percent okay but  but listen here's the biggest thing i'll  say about these letters  is you just need to keep sending them  and be consistent you know if you just  send out  50 letters we send how many of these do  we send that way like 25 30 a week  we send about 25 a week a week that's  not a lot of letters  but it's consistency and consistency  will win this race  so if you want to get a deal in property  or if you want to be a full-time  property investor developer whatever  rather than being like i'm going to go  all that like crazy like you see me do  on the financial freedom challenges  that's okay but my everyday life is  relaxed and chilled i'm just  consistently doing work in the  background  yeah i think that makes sense and are  you typically  looking for properties with planning or  without planning  okay so it depends on what the deal is  so if it's a house  a negative equity house then planning  obviously doesn't come into it  your question is very much tailored  towards property development because  right now that's  more of what we're doing um so if it's a  property development let's say a piece  of land  and we're looking to we're looking to  build our build on a piece of land  generally speaking firstly you don't  necessarily even know  what the situation is because we don't  do loads of due diligence on the site  before sending the letter but generally  speaking we're looking for properties  without planning  the profits in the planning so if if  there's a piece of land and it's already  got planning  that's okay if it's already got planning  it's going to sell at a premium  so we've been looking to buy land  without planning i mean we  you know i mean um but both it depends  there's lots of money and it's all good  yeah no it makes sense yeah um and  if you were advising someone on how to  get started in property development  yeah what would you start with small  deals start with small deals  build up to big deals you're going to  mess up on your first deal  so so you want to start with you with a  small bit and you've got like a list of  questions do you want to just read them  out too  yeah yeah my last question is  what do you do if planning is declined  if planning is declined  um okay so when you offer on the  property in the first place to buy it  generally speaking you're gonna make  three types of offers offer number one  is going to be a straightforward  purchase on the land as it is with no  panic  let's say the piece of land is um you  know half an acre  it's got no planning you have a good  idea if you think the planning is going  to get accepted or not because of the  what the area is doing  because of the the pattern you might  have an idea of the council is there a  shortage of houses in that area so  you're going to have as an experienced  property developer a bit of an idea if  you're going to get planning  so you can say look i'll buy it straight  off you and you'll offer maybe 200  000 pounds which is not a massive amount  of money for half a day because  certainly not where where we live in  fact how much did we offer on that piece  of land right near my house down the  road  we're 80 000 okay 80 000. 8000 how big  was that  that was for an acre of land an acre  right so that's  are you sure but nearly nearly an acre  okay so  80 grams for an acre is not  a lot of money so if you're going to buy  so there's three types of offers one  offer is just a quick  you know quick um bike cash offer if  you can't get planning it doesn't matter  that much because you only paid a